{"title":"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/5/335977913022df1fb3a473f90be2743ad42ada67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=mx+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"90\" height=\"16\" /> be the image when the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/9/4297b6316acd2187c9538e2cdc1cfd697a8d4092.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-3y+11=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"124\" height=\"16\" /> is reflected across the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-axis. The value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/d/24d1e3a8b630344119e20a6d87c9b37cc7fdd1bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/c/15c1baed866a8846d12a80534d343f5075eaece7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A) -6} \\quad \\text{(B) } -5\\quad \\text{(C) } -4\\quad \\text{(D) } -3\\quad \\text{(E) } -2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"357\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First we want to put this is slope-intercept form, so we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/c/a7c83d60e8f47aca1765e93d3b724912ab53f5fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\dfrac{1}{3}x+\\dfrac{11}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"103\" height=\"38\" />. When we reflect a line across the x-axis, the line's x-intercept stays the same, while the y-intercept and the slope are additive inverses of the original line. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/d/24d1e3a8b630344119e20a6d87c9b37cc7fdd1bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> is the sum of the slope and the y-intercept, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/5/d55c7e5f0657e2307f6c748b6564f92ecbb04530.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\dfrac{1}{3}-\\dfrac{11}{3}=\\boxed{-4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"131\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME\" title=\"1992 AHSME\">1992 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1992 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1992 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1992\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" tit